# PART 5: MAKE THUNDERHEAD SPAWN IN OTHER GAME MODES

This is extremely important.

Currently, the Thunderhead boss should not be restricted to special campaign missions.

I want the boss to actually spawn and function in other playable game modes.

Integrate it into the existing game mode and spawn management systems.

Do not simply display it in a menu.

It must actually spawn, navigate the battlefield, detect targets, attack, receive damage, and be destroyable.

## 1. Skirmish mode

Add a boss encounter configuration to Skirmish.

Allow the player to select:

- No boss.
- Siege.
- Cataclysm.
- Stormbringer.
- Fortress.
- Blackout.
- Random boss.

Allow adjustable settings for:
- Boss health multiplier.
- Boss damage multiplier.
- Boss movement speed.
- Boss spawn distance.
- Boss aggression.
- Boss attack frequency.

The player should be able to launch a normal skirmish with a boss included.

The boss should behave as an additional enemy faction threat.

## 2. Survival mode

Add Thunderhead bosses to the wave system.

Bosses should appear during special waves.

Example progression:

- Wave 1-3: Normal enemy units.
- Wave 4: Larger enemy formation.
- Wave 5: First Thunderhead encounter.
- Wave 6-9: Increasing enemy difficulty.
- Wave 10: More dangerous boss variant.
- Later waves: Random Thunderhead variants and additional enemy formations.

Make the boss encounters progressively harder.

Do not spawn multiple enormous bosses immediately unless the player has deliberately selected an extreme difficulty.

The wave system should account for the boss's health, damage, and attack patterns.

## 3. Free Roam

Make Thunderhead bosses capable of spawning naturally in the open world.

They should behave like roaming high-threat military units.

Spawn them:
- At distant battlefield locations.
- Near enemy-controlled territory.
- In specialized artillery zones.
- During random high-threat encounters.

The player should occasionally discover one through reconnaissance, minimap signals, distant explosions, or radio warnings.

Some bosses should roam between locations.

Others should remain in patrol areas until they detect the player.

Do not spawn them directly on top of the player.

Create a minimum spawn distance and proper terrain validation.

## 4. Training mode

Add a boss testing option.

Allow the player to spawn:
- Any individual Thunderhead variant.
- A selected boss ultimate.
- Different boss health values.
- Different movement speeds.
- Different aggression settings.

Make it useful for testing weapons and procedural animations.

## 5. Campaign mode

Preserve all existing scripted boss missions.

The new movement system and ultimate abilities must work in campaign encounters.

Also allow Thunderhead variants to appear in suitable campaign missions as additional threats.

