# FINAL EXPECTED RESULT

The updated game should now feature a new player-controlled long-range artillery mech and five completely revamped Thunderhead boss variants.

The M-09 COLOSSUS should allow players to experience heavy artillery combat firsthand, with ballistic targeting, ammunition choices, powerful recoil, and a special artillery barrage.

Thunderhead should become a much more unpredictable and dangerous threat.

It should be enormous, but surprisingly fast.

It should rapidly cross the battlefield using its massive procedural legs, reposition itself, acquire targets, and unleash devastating long-range mortar attacks.

Its ultimate abilities should have their own recognizable animations, sound design, camera movements, and cinematic sequences.

Most importantly, Thunderhead should no longer be limited to campaign missions. It must actually appear and function in Skirmish, Survival, Free Roam, and Training.

**FINAL DESIGN DIRECTION:**

The player now has access to mobile artillery, but the enemy has an enormous, high-speed strategic artillery platform.

The player can bombard the battlefield from a distance, but the Thunderhead can hunt them down while doing the same.

Make artillery combat feel like a battle of positioning, prediction, timing, and overwhelming mechanical firepower.